          "text": "{\"regions\":{\"r2\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 81. \u0915\u094d\u0935\u091a\u093f\u0924\u094d\u2014may better be taken as an adv. of time; at one\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"time, at another, \u092d\u0942\u092e\u093f\u0936\u093e\u092f\u0940 is a better reading than \u092d\u0942\u092e\u094c \u0936\u093e\u092f\u0940 as\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"keeping up symmetry. \u0936\u093e\u0932\u094d\u092f\u094b\u0926\u0928\u0966\u2014Having a liking for S'\u00e2li ( a\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"superior kind of paddy ) only. \u0915\u0928\u094d\u0925\u093e\u0927\u093e\u0930\u0940\u2014One wearing a wallet.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"\u092e\u0928\u0938\u094d\u0935\u0940\u2014from \u092e\u0928\u0938\u094d + \u0935\u093f\u0928\u093f\u0903 high-souled, also wise. \u0935\u093f\u0928\u094d shows\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"\u092a\u094d\u0930\u093e\u0936\u0938\u094d\u0924\u094d\u092f. \u0915\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0925\u0940 ( \u0915\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f\u0902 \u0905\u0930\u094d\u0925\u092f\u0924\u0947 \u0907\u0924\u093f ) One that seeks to gain\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"his object. This as well as \u0915\u0928\u094d\u0925\u093e\u0927\u093e\u0930\u0940 and \u0936\u093e\u0915\u093e\u0939\u093e\u0930\u0940 are formed by\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"affixing \u0907\u0928\u094d ( \u0923\u093f\u0928\u093f\u0903 ) by \u0938\u0941\u092a\u094d\u092f\u091c\u093e\u0924\u094c \u0923\u093f\u0928\u093f\u0938\u094d\u0924\u093e\u091a\u094d\u091b\u0940\u0932\u094d\u092f\u0947 ( \u0907\u0928\u094d is added\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":10,\"text\":\"to a root in the sense of \u2018in the habit of\u2019 when it is preceded\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":11,\"text\":\"by a noun not denoting a class). \u0915\u093e\u0930\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0925\u0940 may also betaken\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":12,\"text\":\"as in the com.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit characters and transliteration diacritics are indistinct.\"},\"r3\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 82. \u0909\u092a\u0936\u092e\u2014Subduing the passions, tranquillity. \u092a\u094d\u0930\u092d\u0935\u093f\u0924\u0943\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"One possessing absolute power. This is the only concrete noun\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"used in the sloka for \u092a\u094d\u0930\u092d\u0935\u0938\u094d\u092f. \u0928\u093f\u0930\u094d\u0935\u094d\u092f\u093e\u091c\u0924\u093e\u2014freedom from hypoc-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"risy. \u0938\u0930\u094d\u0935\u0947\u0937\u093e\u092e\u094d &c.\u2014Some take this to mean \u2018of all persons,\u2019 in\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"which sense \u0905\u092a\u093f would be superfluous. \u0938\u0930\u094d\u0935\u0915\u093e\u0930\u0923\u092e\u094d cause of all\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"i. e. of \u0910\u0936\u094d\u0935\u0930\u094d\u092f, \u0938\u0941\u091c\u0928\u0924\u093e &c. \u0936\u0940\u0932\u2013virtuous or good conduct.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit readings are indistinct.\"},\"r4\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 83. \u0928\u0940\u0924\u093f\u2014The conduct of human affairs, rules of life. \u092f\u0926\u093f\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"\u0935\u093e\u2014is equivalent here to \u0905\u0925\u0935\u093e. \u0928\u094d\u092f\u093e\u092f\u094d\u092f\u093e\u0924\u094d\u2013see sl. 28. supra.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"\u0927\u0940\u0930\u093e\u0903\u2014\u0927\u093f\u092f\u0902 \u092c\u0941\u0926\u094d\u0927\u093f\u092e\u0940\u0930\u092f\u0928\u094d\u0924\u093f \u0938\u0930\u094d\u0935\u0924\u0903 \u092a\u094d\u0930\u0935\u0930\u094d\u0924\u092f\u0928\u094d\u0924\u0940\u0924\u093f \u0964 R\u00e2marshi. The wise.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit etymological explanation is difficult to read.\"},\"r5\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 84. \u0915\u0926\u0930\u094d\u0925\u093f\u0924\u0938\u094d\u092f-p. p. of \u0915\u0926\u0930\u094d\u0925\u092f\u094d denom. fr. \u0915\u0926\u0930\u094d\u0925 ( \u0915\u0941\u0924\u094d\u0938\u093f\u0924\u094b\u093d\u0930\u094d\u0925\u0903 )\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"of one who is despised, afflicted, worried. \u092a\u094d\u0930\u092e\u093e\u0930\u094d\u0937\u094d\u091f\u0941\u092e\u094d\u2014to wipe off\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"completely, to obliterate. Mr. Telang rightly remarks that\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\u0905\u0927\u094b\u092e\u0941\u0916\u0938\u094d\u092f \u0915\u0943\u0924\u0938\u094d\u092f is not a usual construction and that therefore\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":5,\"text\":\"the reading \u0924\u0928\u0942\u0928\u092a\u093e\u0924\u0903 ( see foot-note p. 34 ) is better. This, how-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":6,\"text\":\"ever, is open to another objection; for it involves the \u0926\u094b\u0937\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":7,\"text\":\"\u0905\u092a\u094d\u0930\u092f\u0941\u0915\u094d\u0924\u0924\u094d\u0935, the word \u0924\u0928\u0942\u0928\u092a\u093e\u0924\u094d\u2014though given by the lexicogra-\",\"end\":\"hyphen\"},{\"n\":8,\"text\":\"phers for \u2018fire, being hardly, if ever, used by the poets. The fig.\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":9,\"text\":\"is \u0926\u0943\u0937\u094d\u091f\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"Some Sanskrit words are indistinct, particularly on the first line.\"},\"r6\":{\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"Sl. 85. \u0928 \u0932\u0941\u0928\u0928\u094d\u0924\u093f \u2018cut or wound\u2019, or pierce. \u0915\u091f\u093e\u0915\u094d\u0937\u0935\u093f\u0936\u093f\u0916\u093e\u0903\u2014\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":2,\"text\":\"arrows in the form of glances. \u0915\u0943\u0936\u093e\u0928\u0941\u0903-\u0915\u0943\u0936\u092f\u0924\u093f that which reduces\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":3,\"text\":\"size; hence fire; \u0915\u0943\u0936\u094d+\u0906\u0928\u0941 ( \u0915 ). Construe \u092f\u0938\u094d\u092f \u091a\u093f\u0924\u094d\u0924\u0902 \u0915\u093e\u0928\u094d\u0924\u093e\u0966 \u0928\",\"end\":\"space\"},{\"n\":4,\"text\":\"\u0916\u0928\u0928\u094d\u0924\u093f \u0966\u0924\u093e\u092a\u0903 \u0928 \u0926\u0939\u0924\u093f and so on.\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":true,\"note\":\"The Sanskrit grammatical derivation and final quotation are somewhat unclear.\"},\"r1\":{\"type\":\"page_number\",\"lines\":[{\"n\":1,\"text\":\"( 32 )\",\"end\":\"space\"}],\"uncertain\":false,\"note\":null}},\"units\":[{\"id\":\"u1\",\"type\":\"notes\",\"number\":null,\"label\":null,\"open_start\":true,\"open_end\":true,\"children\":[\"u2\",\"u3\",\"u4\",\"u5\",\"u6\"]},{\"id\":\"u2\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"81\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r2\"]},{\"id\":\"u3\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"82\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r3\"]},{\"id\":\"u4\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"83\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r4\"]},{\"id\":\"u5\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"84\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r5\"]},{\"id\":\"u6\",\"type\":\"stanza_note\",\"number\":\"85\",\"label\":null,\"open_start\":false,\"open_end\":false,\"children\":[\"r6\"]}],\"flows\":[{\"flow\":\"main\",\"units\":[\"u1\"]},{\"flow\":\"notes\",\"units\":[]}],\"relations\":[]}"
